# GigaMeter research

Methodology lives in the track docs under `docs-site/`. Numbers live in `SpatialConfig` and on the Parameters page. Decisions live in `docs/adr/` (the landing site). Do not put spatial weights, DBSCAN settings, or distance cutoffs in these rules.

Plan first, and make no edits until the plan is approved. Ask clarifying questions. Change a parameter only when an edge case shows it fails.

Never take a location from IP. `detected_latitude` and `detected_longitude` come only from Google Wi-Fi geolocation. Never fill them from `client_info`. Follow [ADR 0007](../../docs/adr/0007-data-handling-public-repo.md).

A method change needs a Research Log entry and a Parameters page update. Never bump `mike` outside a freeze ([ADR 0003](../../docs/adr/0003-versioning-and-freeze.md)).

Time is facility-local, from `created_timestamp_utc` and the school location. Never use the device clock or the IP time zone ([ADR 0011](../../docs/adr/0011-operational-hours.md), [ADR 0012](../../docs/adr/0012-time-basis.md)).
